mode: "100644"
text: "# Recycling 2026 reality — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (platform originality rules and reach norms shift).*\n\n## Why recycling works (the case)\n- **Most of your audience never saw the original.** Only ~5–10% of a network sees a given post; an\n  estimated **80%+ miss your initial posts**. New followers never saw it at all.\n- **Algorithms can re-push proven content.** Reposts/revisions of pieces that worked before have a\n  good chance of being surfaced again in their refreshed form. **LinkedIn now values relevance over\n  recency** — strong evergreen posts keep gaining traction long after publishing.\n- **Evergreen has a long half-life.** Frameworks, tips, and core messaging stay useful for months/\n  years; repetition strengthens brand recall (especially ideas that need several exposures to land).\n\n## The hard constraint — refresh, not duplicate\n- **Meta's Original Content rules** (enforced since July 2025; verify-quarterly): **penalties for\n  unoriginal/duplicate content** — reduced reach (applied account-wide, not just the offending post),\n  demonetization, and \"non-recommendable\" status for accounts repeatedly reusing material; Instagram\n  **redirects viewers to the original** version of a clip rather than showing reposts; other-platform\n  watermarks penalized. Reaction videos / trend participation / added-take content are exempt. **Quality over volume** — fewer original\n  posts outperform more low-effort reposts.\n- Net: **identical reposting is risky.** Treat recycling as **editing, not duplication.** \"Never\n  repeat the same opening line twice.\"\n\n## What's recyclable vs not\n- **Recycle:** evergreen + proven — practical tips, frameworks, timeless case studies, product guides,\n  customer success, core brand messaging. Also **strong-but-underseen** pieces that deserved more.\n- **Don't recycle:** time-bound — events, seasonal promos, outdated news, trend-jacks. Always check an\n  old post still aligns with current facts and trends before reusing.\n\n## Cadence + spacing (verify-quarterly)\n- Recycle a top performer roughly **every 90–120 days** — long enough that the audience has moved on\n  and new followers have arrived.\n- Space assets across the calendar; **don't dump** a backlog at once. Sprinkle recycled pieces among\n  native new content so the feed doesn't read as repetitive.\n- Let **native analytics** drive which assets re-enter the queue (data over guessing).\n\n## Refresh tactics (quick wins)\nRewrite the first sentence · swap the opening visual · tighten the first five seconds · update dates/\nprices/stats/claims · flip the format (carousel ↔ Reel ↔ text) · adapt to season (\"Summer Posting\nGuide\") · re-check compliance/endorsement language. **Change one major variable per variant** (hook,\nproof point, or CTA) so you can learn what moved the metric.\n"
